      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s claim that the expression was “later used more loosely for reckless or blindly aggressive behavior” is only partially supported. The packet supports a “fanciful” use for “the blind impulsive aggressiveness of epileptic furor,” but it does not support a general “more loosely” meaning as reckless or blindly aggressive behavior in general (it also adds a separate colloquial sense about talking/writing ignorantly)."
